\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces C1 evidence under a common absolute noise level, $480$ paired trials per point or cell. (a)~Matched accuracy (solid) against the free-Jones PEB (dashed) for the three receiver modes. (b)~Paired inlier-conditional efficiency ratio; the band is $\pm 2\%$ and the scalar curve leaves the plotted range at the two printed values. (c)--(e)~Resolution probability versus delay separation and Jones overlap at $-10$~dB; the dashed line is the reference scene's minimum cascaded-delay separation. Full EVS retains cross-panel polarimetric separability; reduced modes become overlap sensitive.}}{12}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c1_combined}{{2}{12}{}{}{}}
