\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces External benchmark with method-consistent continuous refinement, $960$ shared-realization trials per SNR, comparing the proposed MKSC-GI+CCOP-JVP, range-scaled 4-D Jones-VP, ALS-CPD with joint mapping, VBI/SBL with joint refinement, and near-field OMP--SAGE--WLS methods. Each column asks one question of position (top) and of the clock or its reconstruction (bottom): precision inside the basin, a tail-sensitive statistic, and the failure rate. (b)~p99 is nearest-rank; the shaded region is the $0.1$-m inlier threshold. (d)~The CEB reference is the median bound of Section~\ref {subsec:res_setup} scaled by $\sigma $. The dotted line in~(c) and~(f) is one trial in $960$, hollow markers on it being exact zeros.}}{15}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:benchmark_combined}{{3}{15}{}{}{}}
